# Testing Philosophy (all apps)

**Test real code. No mocks unless physically impossible.**

**`vi.mock` is FORBIDDEN unless there is no other way.** The only acceptable reason to mock is **third-party integrations that are not available in the test environment** (external SaaS APIs with no local equivalent). Everything internal — feature logic, hooks, helpers, utils, state — runs real. This also keeps tests fast by avoiding network calls to external services.

When a new third-party integration needs mocking, **build a reusable mock helper** in the app's testing directory (`src/testing/mocks/` on the backend, `src/testing/helpers/` on the frontend) so every test file imports a single function instead of duplicating setup. Keep mock helpers focused, typed, and documented so future tests get mocking for free.

## Rules shared by every test file

1. **NEVER import vitest** — globals are available.
2. **No `any` types** — type mocks properly, e.g. `vi.fn<(args) => ReturnType>()`.
3. **Tests must be independent** — each test creates its own data and cleans up after itself.
4. **Every test MUST use `// Arrange`, `// Act`, `// Assert` comments** to clearly separate setup, execution, and verification. Skip `// Arrange` only when there is no setup.
5. **No `try/catch` for error assertions** — use `expect().rejects`.

App-specific conventions live in the backend and frontend testing rules.
